<!--
    An inline system call (`svc`) lifts to a CALLOTHER with no register inputs
    and no output, so the r0 a function sets up for it still holds that value
    afterwards. `pair` returns the two argument registers it set up as a register pair, and
    `after` doubles its argument: it reads back the r0 it saved, not the result.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 flow-classification.
    P0 assertion:      option syscallregs off|auto|on  (default auto).

    Source (clang -O2 -target armv7-linux-gnueabi -c, the .text bytes verbatim below):

        static __attribute__((noinline)) void use2(int a, int b)
          { asm volatile("" :: "r"(a), "r"(b)); }
        int pair(int a, int b) {
          register int r0 asm("r0") = b; register int r1 asm("r1") = a;
          register int r7 asm("r7") = 4;
          asm volatile("svc 0" : "+r"(r0) : "r"(r1), "r"(r7) : "memory");
          return r0;
        }
        int after(int x) {
          register int r0 asm("r0"); register int r7 asm("r7") = 20;
          asm volatile("svc 0" : "=r"(r0) : "r"(r7) : "memory");
          if (r0 < 0) return -1;
          return r0 + x;
        }
        int fence(int a) { asm volatile("dmb ish" ::: "memory"); return a; }
        int discard(int a, int b) {
          register int r0 asm("r0") = b + 1; register int r1 asm("r1") = a * 3;
          register int r7 asm("r7") = 4;
          asm volatile("svc 0" : "+r"(r0) : "r"(r1), "r"(r7) : "memory");
          return 7;
        }
        void keep(int fd, int buf) {
          register int r0 asm("r0") = fd + 1; register int r1 asm("r1") = buf * 3;
          register int r7 asm("r7") = 4;
          asm volatile("svc 0" : "+r"(r0) : "r"(r1), "r"(r7) : "memory");
          use2(r0, r1);
        }

    Pass 1 (option syscallregs on) gives the svc its effects: it writes r0,
    and it reads the number register r7 and then the argument registers in
    order, up to the first one the function did not write on every path to
    it.  Pass 2 (option syscallregs off) is the old model, and so is pass 3,
    the default `auto`: it acts only on an image the loader identified as a
    program for an operating system's user space, which a bare byte chunk is
    not.  rd_into_global is GH-856: it stores x + 7 to sink, asks read()
    to overwrite sink with svc 0, reloads sink and returns (x + 7) * 5 + sink.
    The on pass preserves both the store and the post-call load; off folds
    the stale store into that load and incorrectly returns (x + 7) * 6.
    fence is the control: its barrier is a CALLOTHER too,
    and nothing about it changes.
    discard throws the result away and returns 7; the kernel leaves r1 alone, so
    the argument in r1 still reaches the return, and a value the call reads as an
    argument is not a returned half.  keep passes the result and the r1 it kept
    to use2; the call reading r1 does not stop it being use2's second argument.
    after keeps x in r1 across the svc but never writes r0, so the call reads
    r7 alone: r1 is not printed as the first argument.
-->
